# SEAM governing documents — standing SHA-256 pins (AM-009).
#
# Verified live against the working tree 2026-08-03.
# Encoding: UTF-8, no BOM, LF line endings, single trailing newline.
# .gitattributes sets -text on these four paths and on this file (AF-007, extended by AM-026 on
# 2026-08-03 — before that date docs/ was NOT covered and committing any governing document would
# have rewritten LF to CRLF and broken all four pins at once). Verify with:
#     git check-attr text -- <path>        # must report "unset", i.e. -text applied
#
# Verify:  python tools/hooks/verify_pins.py
#          (also runs automatically as a pre-commit hook)
#
# On a mismatch, decide WHICH CASE before acting:
#   KNOWN SUPERSESSION  — the doc changed via a logged amendment. Update the pin,
#                         archive the superseded hash below, commit both together.
#   UNEXPLAINED DRIFT   — no amendment covers it. Stop and investigate.
#   ENCODING            — a CRLF save or altered trailing newline. Restore LF;
#                         do NOT edit the pin to match.
# Never edit this list to silence a mismatch you do not understand.

